**Where it is used.** The `@semio/ui`, `@semio/animation` and Studio icon registries render Solar components for shared controls, transport, editor actions, units and legal glyphs.

**Vendored Solar artwork.** These `@semio/ui` glyphs copy Solar geometry into `@semio/ui`'s `dist` rather than rendering a package component. Source: <https://github.com/saoudi-h/solar-icons/tree/main/packages/core/svgs>.

- LineDuotone `sidebar-open`, `sidebar-close`, `panels-top-left` and `videocamera-off` (`src/icons/sidebar-open.tsx`, `sidebar-close.tsx`, `panels-top-left.tsx`, `videocamera-off.tsx`).
- `add-file` and `exclamation-mark`, from the catalogue SVGs (`src/icons/shared-glyphs.tsx`).
- `hexagon`, adapted from BoxMinimalistic's outer contour without its internal edges (`src/icons/shared-glyphs.tsx`).

**Modifications.** Rendered as React components at Semio's sizes, recoloured through `currentColor`; the `hexagon` adaptation above removes internal edges. Semio's own Solar-style glyphs are drawn to the same 24-unit grid and stroke weight.

### Supplied artwork — adapted Solar glyphs and original Semio artwork

These `@semio/ui` glyphs render SVG artwork supplied to the project, with its geometry, transforms and opacity preserved and colours inheriting `currentColor`:

`robot`, `folder-open`, `folder-closed`, `box-plus`, `hand`, `user`, `moon`, `sun-moon`, `replace`, `rotate-3d`, `data-binary`, `save`, `time-display-milliseconds`, `time-display-seconds`, `time-display-frames`, `time-display-seconds-frames`, `time-display-ticks`, `sort-updated`, `sphere`.

Each glyph in this set is one of two things:

- **An adaptation of a Solar icon**, made for consistency with the rest of Semio's set. Such a glyph is adapted from **"Solar Icons" by [480 Design](https://www.figma.com/community/file/1166831539721848736)**, licensed under [CC BY 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), and has been modified from the Solar original.
- **Original Semio artwork** drawn in the Solar style. Such a glyph is Semio's own and carries no third-party attribution: a visual style is not licensable, so a glyph drawn to match Solar's look without deriving from a Solar file owes Solar nothing.

The Figma "Semio UI Library" file mirrors these icons and carries the same attribution on its Icons page.
